@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Native theme update repair for ghostty-web 0.4.0
+
+Source: coder/ghostty-web v0.4.0 / 9e4e126d89ac3537d2b2ebec075849851566de9f.
+Ghostty submodule: 5714ed07a1012573261b7b7e3ed2add9c1504496.
+Compiler: Zig 0.15.2, x86_64-linux archive SHA-256
+02aa270f183da276e5b5920b1dac44a63f1a49e55050ebde3aecc9eb82f93239.
+
+Apply OPENCLAW_WASM_BINDINGS.patch with git apply --unidiff-zero to the
+ghostty-web checkout. Initialize its
+Ghostty submodule and apply upstream patches/ghostty-wasm-api.patch there, then
+apply OPENCLAW_WASM_PALETTE.patch with git apply --unidiff-zero. Build only the native module:
+
+    zig build lib-vt -Dtarget=wasm32-freestanding -Doptimize=ReleaseSmall -j2
+
+Copy zig-out/bin/ghostty-vt.wasm to the ghostty-web checkout root. Install its
+frozen bun.lock and run build:lib. The supplied build config emits ordinary
+module declarations: the pinned declaration-rollup tool cannot follow Promise.
+The declaration generator emits explicit .js relative specifiers for NodeNext.
+Source typecheck, generated declaration consumers, ESM and CommonJS loaders must
+pass. Preserve the existing clipboard-success and listener-disposal repairs,
+which are included in the bindings source patch.
+
+The native host setter changes palette/default-color state directly, not the
+PTY stream. UI-owned first-16 overrides reset to the new default palette;
+extended application palette overrides remain. OSC 104 and OSC 110/111 reset
+to the active UI theme. Normal application OSC colors delegate to Ghostty's
+existing state owner, with terminal-owned parser allocations and teardown.
+
+The canvas paints resolved native RGB backgrounds, including literal black.
+Both generated JavaScript formats embed the rebuilt WASM. Original standalone
+WASM exports retain upstream bytes for explicit alternate-loader contracts;
+OpenClaw uses the default embedded loader. No binary is applied through pnpm's
+text patcher. Original upstream license notices remain unchanged.
+
+Rebuilt embedded WASM SHA-256: c4fe68c8a89b044500985210122b09ee42b5dcd2130b090ae69378d7553250dc
+
+pnpm preserves CRLF context lines in the existing index declaration and adds a
+final newline to one declaration map. Verify normalized declaration content and
+exact runtime/native hashes after a fresh frozen install.
